{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And he said.</b> [Pharaoh means:] May YHWH be with you — as you say, 'with us.'" "And the meaning of 'see that evil is before your faces' is that the evil is near you, and it is before your faces. Joined to this meaning: for it is that which you seek, so it is fitting that I do thus. Now Pharaoh thought that they wanted to flee. Know that Moses our master did not say to Pharaoh that they would return unless he lied; rather he said that they would go a distance of three days. And the Egyptians' understanding was that they would return, because he lent them, and for another reason: had Pharaoh given them permission to go and not return, he would not have pursued them. And HaShem commanded to do thus, until he would pursue them and drown. This is explicit: 'they shall turn back and encamp before Pi-haChirot' (Exodus 14:2). And one must not question the deeds of HaShem, for He did everything in wisdom, though it is hidden from the eyes of the wise. Now in David's words: 'when you hear the sound of marching in the tops of the baca trees, then bestir yourself, for then YHWH will go out before you to strike the camp of the Philistines' (2 Samuel 5:24)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:11.124158437Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}